# Data fetching and shared state

- Keep remote data fetching and shared or global data management in Pinia stores, not inside pages or presentational components.
- Pages and components render UI, hold local UI-only state, and call store actions.
- When a page owns async entity state (loading, saving, lists that may be reused), create or extend a store first.
- Reserve local component refs for ephemeral UI such as toggles, open state, and one-off feedback.
- Async store actions return `{ data, error }` and reset `loading` in `finally`.
